# f1 = Asks, f2 = Reads, f3 = Stores, f4 = Falls
# `never` is undefined for all to see, so one of the two edges that are written into the block behind the `if` is taken, and both come out of blocks that are entered. The scan follows `this` under the name `self`:
# the hand-over is no leaving, and `second` is filled for those outside the construction. Inside it, `self` is the object that is being made: `second` is not there yet.
# The walk counted the written edges for itself and took `self` for an object from elsewhere: "second" in self was true, typeof self.second was "number", and self.second = seed overwrote and listed no key.
# In the last, the case that is taken falls through into the next, which the switch names too.
# RUN(ASKS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# ASKS: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="second" receivers=[L0]
# RUN(READS): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# READS: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key="second" receivers=[L1]
# RUN(STORES): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# STORES: = PutSlotOrAdd {{*}}key="second" receivers=[L2]
# STORES: = PutSlot {{*}}key="second" receivers=[L2]
# RUN(FALLS): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# FALLS: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="second" receivers=[L3]
# RUN(SCAN): summary f1 mechanisms=all
# SCAN: still-being-made v7 = v0
# What those outside are told stands.
